1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,440
Everything so far has been desk research.

2
00:00:03,490 --> 00:00:05,670
The next milestone isn't building more.

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:11,660
It's finding out whether the problem, and my product, hold up with real families and real hosts.

4
00:00:11,710 --> 00:00:14,680
So the roadmap is four weeks, around one hospital:

5
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,715
Aster Medcity, in Cheranalloor.

6
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:26,115
Aster already offers accommodation assistance to international patients, so The Veedu has to add value beyond a list of nearby rooms.

7
00:00:26,165 --> 00:00:30,901
Amrita, in Ponekkara, is the second cluster — but only after the first pilot.

8
00:00:31,801 --> 00:00:33,771
I'm testing five hypotheses.

9
00:00:33,821 --> 00:00:39,861
That families struggle to compare stays by hospital distance, needs, duration and availability.

10
00:00:39,911 --> 00:00:43,291
That they need clearer information before contacting a host.

11
00:00:43,341 --> 00:00:46,181
That some prefer a home to a hotel for longer stays.

12
00:00:46,231 --> 00:00:51,381
That hosts will keep their details accurate in exchange for relevant enquiries.

13
00:00:51,431 --> 00:00:54,791
And that The Veedu actually reduces the effort of shortlisting.

14
00:00:54,841 --> 00:00:56,183
None of these is proven.

15
00:00:57,083 --> 00:00:59,733
Before testing anything, I checked the live site.

16
00:00:59,783 --> 00:01:05,013
Today it has no published listings, and the location picker lists areas, not hospitals.

17
00:01:05,063 --> 00:01:07,163
Aster Medcity isn't in it.

18
00:01:07,213 --> 00:01:14,705
So week one also means adding the hospital, and onboarding a few host-confirmed properties, so there's something real to test.

19
00:01:15,605 --> 00:01:17,145
Week one is discovery.

20
00:01:17,195 --> 00:01:29,135
Eight to twelve people who've recently arranged a stay for a family member's treatment in Kochi, and five to eight hosts, recruited through my own network and host referrals, not through the hospital.

21
00:01:29,185 --> 00:01:32,638
The questions are about what they actually did, not what they'd like.

22
00:01:33,538 --> 00:01:36,788
Week two tests the real website with six to eight people.

23
00:01:36,838 --> 00:01:39,258
Find a place near Aster for five nights.

24
00:01:39,308 --> 00:01:40,698
Compare two properties.

25
00:01:40,748 --> 00:01:42,568
Work out how to contact the host.

26
00:01:42,618 --> 00:01:44,648
Then tell me what's still missing.

27
00:01:44,698 --> 00:01:48,584
I'll watch without guiding, and a successful click isn't booking intent.

28
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:51,884
Weeks three and four are a concierge pilot.

29
00:01:51,934 --> 00:01:59,574
I'll confirm ten to fifteen properties with their hosts, record real distance and travel time, and publish only what's been checked.

30
00:01:59,624 --> 00:02:04,679
Enquiries go through the existing WhatsApp flow, and a simple spreadsheet tracks every one.

31
00:02:05,579 --> 00:02:08,299
Success is defined before the pilot starts.

32
00:02:08,349 --> 00:02:10,979
Five of eight participants shortlist without help.

33
00:02:11,029 --> 00:02:13,889
At least ten properties with host-confirmed details.

34
00:02:13,939 --> 00:02:16,469
Hosts saying the enquiries are useful.

35
00:02:16,519 --> 00:02:19,780
These are small-sample signals, not market validation.

36
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:23,950
At the end of week four, the evidence decides the next step.

37
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,120
If people find stays but don't trust them, verification comes first.

38
00:02:28,170 --> 00:02:30,760
If they can't find them, search and distance do.

39
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:33,850
If hosts don't respond, onboarding is the problem.

40
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:39,090
If families prefer the hospital's own recommendations, The Veedu should complement them.

41
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:43,747
And if there's no real value over today's search, I go back to the problem itself.

42
00:02:44,647 --> 00:02:48,067
The next milestone for The Veedu is not scaling the platform.

43
00:02:48,117 --> 00:02:58,067
It's proving that a small group of families can find suitable accommodation with less uncertainty, and that local hosts can reliably fulfil those enquiries.

44
00:02:58,117 --> 00:03:07,056
Before expanding to more hospitals, or automating the whole workflow, the product needs evidence from real users and real accommodation providers.
